Step by step
1. Copy code 1 from Markdown into Blender -> Scripting
2. Analyse data given in the csv. file generated from the python console 
3. If missing data, follow your matching path in the BPMN diagram 
4. Our matching patch was to import a generated csv file with indoor conditions to blender. Step 4 is then to copy code 2 from Markdown into Blender -> Scripting. 
5. Now run code 1 again and read the csv file to control that the imported data is now existing in the model 
6. Control with Danish Standard if values are within the criteria
7. If not within required values, suggest an improvement or addition for passive or active cooling/heating. 
